              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "I cannot directly purchase tickets or access your personal and payment information. However, I can walk you through the entire process and provide the direct links so you can book your trip quickly. \n\nBecause today is Sunday, June 7, 2026, **\"next Friday\" refers to June 12, 2026**. \n\nHere is exactly how to book your return (round-trip) train ticket from Boston to New York:\n\n### 1. Where to Book\nThe primary passenger train service between Boston and New York is **Amtrak**. You should book directly on the [Amtrak Website](https://www.amtrak.com) or download the Amtrak app.\n\n### 2. Enter Your Trip Details\nWhen booking, you will need to input the following details:\n*   **From:** Boston, MA \u2013 South Station (BOS) or Back Bay (BBY). *(Tip: Starting your trip at South Station is recommended, as it is the first stop and gives you the best chance of finding good overhead luggage space and seats if you travel coach).*\n*   **To:** New York, NY \u2013 Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP).\n*   **Trip Type:** Round Trip (Return)\n*   **Depart Date:** Friday, June 12, 2026\n*   **Return Date:** *Input your preferred return date (e.g., Sunday, June 14, 2026, or the same day).*\n\n### 3. Choose Your Train Type\nAmtrak offers two main types of trains for this route:\n*   **Northeast Regional:** Takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. It is the most affordable option, with a standard Coach class and a Business class. \n*   **Acela (High-Speed):** Takes about **3 hours and 30 minutes**. It is faster but more expensive and only offers Business and First Class.\n\n### 4. General Pricing & Booking Tips\n*   **Book ASAP:** Friday afternoons and Sunday evenings are peak travel times. Ticket prices on these days rise significantly the closer you get to the departure date.\n*   **Discounts:** If you are a student, senior, active military, or traveling with children, look for the \"Discounts\" dropdown on the passenger page to apply a 10% to 50% discount.\n*   **Alternative comparison:** If you want to compare Amtrak schedules alongside bus options (like Greyhound or Peter Pan) for a lower-cost alternative, you can use [Wanderu](https://www.wanderu.com) or [Omio](https://www.omio.com). \n\nYou can complete your reservation securely on [Amtrak.com](https://www.amtrak.com) using a credit card, Apple Pay, Google Pay, or PayPal. Safe travels!",
